mm: a lazy pagemap's metadata pages' structures left unmade

A pagemap whose pages' structures lie in its own memory (an altmap) has the structures of
that memory's pages made too, as its range moves to ZONE_DEVICE (memmap_init_range()): a
4,096th of the device, each structure its own (each lists itself), so a snapshot keeps
every one. For a 64 GiB virtio-fs DAX window that is 18 MiB its guest's boot writes and
each template of it keeps (shards' PM M306), where the window's own pages' structures are
made as its ranges are first mapped (0011). Those pages are the pagemap's metadata: no pfn
of it hands them out (pfn_first(), pgmap_pfn_valid()), memory failure leaves them be
("device metadata space is not recoverable"), and x86's and arm64's vmemmap give them back
by the altmap without reading their structures. Where the pagemap's owner makes its pages'
structures (PGMAP_LAZY_MEMMAP), they are left unmade.

--- a/mm/memremap.c
+++ b/mm/memremap.c
@@ -227,8 +227,18 @@ static int pagemap_range(struct dev_pagemap *pgmap, struct mhp_params *params,
 		struct zone *zone;
 
 		zone = &NODE_DATA(nid)->node_zones[ZONE_DEVICE];
+		/*
+		 * shards: the structures of the pages that hold the pages' structures (the
+		 * altmap's) are left unmade where the pgmap's owner makes its pages' own
+		 * (PGMAP_LAZY_MEMMAP): those pages are its metadata, which no pfn of it hands out
+		 * (pfn_first(), pgmap_pfn_valid()), no memory failure reads ("device metadata
+		 * space") and its vmemmap gives back by its altmap; made, they took a 4,096th of
+		 * the device, each page's its own.
+		 */
 		move_pfn_range_to_zone(zone, PHYS_PFN(range->start),
-				PHYS_PFN(range_len(range)), params->altmap,
+				PHYS_PFN(range_len(range)),
+				(pgmap->flags & PGMAP_LAZY_MEMMAP) ? NULL :
+								     params->altmap,
 				MIGRATE_MOVABLE, false);
 	}
 
